I use Textpad for editing.  It has C syntax highlighting and regular
expressions, etc.  I use Cygwin for the compiler, etc.

It wouldn't hurt you to learn vi if you ever have a job using Unix or
Linux, but a Windows editor like Textpad is a lot easier to use.

I think the other people are right.  If you just want to learn C on
Windows you would be better using some sort of integrated
environment.  But, if you want to compile nethack under Windows Cygwin
is pretty easy to get and lots of people use it for Nethack.

